  "body": "### Summary\nLOT-055 (#81) must not call an AQ creation a success without a captured confirmation. Legacy treats the body `\"1\"` as success (`MessagesView.swift:340-399` @ `2440d79`), but no answer of `POST https://aq.super-h.fr/api/addAlerte.php` has been captured, so the AQ create is left out of LOT-055 until this capture exists.\n\n### Scope\n- **This is a public write to a third-party server** (LOT-071 T3): it creates a visible AQ under a pseudo, unauthenticated. The operator decides first whether and where (which topic/message, which pseudo) it may be done; nothing is sent without that decision (AGENTS §0).\n- Wanted, each with status, headers (`Content-Type`, any `Location`/`Set-Cookie` names), raw body bytes:\n  1. a successful create, new AQ (`alerte_qualitay_id=-1`), body built exactly as legacy `aqRequestBody` (field order `alerte_qualitay_id, nom, topic_id, topic_titre, pseudo, post_id, post_url, commentaire`; legacy percent-encoding `A-Za-z0-9._-`, ASCII body with lossy conversion);\n  2. if the operator agrees, one refusal (for example a missing `nom`) to tell a refusal from a success;\n  3. whether `getAlertesByTopic.php` then lists the new AQ (a `T02`-shaped re-read of the same topic).\n- Cookie-less (no forum cookie, as SwiftHFR will send it), no redirect followed. Anonymize per FIXTURES (pseudo → `userN`, member text → `x`).\n- If the operator declines the write, say so here: LOT-055/LOT-134 then ship the create as \"unconfirmed\" only or not at all.\n\n### Wanted by\nLOT-055 (#81, `Refs #81`: create left out), LOT-134 (#224, AQ creation from a message).\n\n### Sources\n`MessagesView.swift:340-437` @ `2440d79` (`createAQ`, `aqRequestBody`, `legacyPercentEncode`); HFR-PROTOCOL §8 `aq.super-h.fr` row; LOT-071 T3 and notice N1.",
